---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base
  title="About — Casual Generosity"
  description="What Casual Generosity is, why it exists, and who built it."
>
  <div class="wrap detail t-Planned">
    <div class="detail-top">
      <a class="back" href={base}>← Home</a>
    </div>

    <div class="detail-head">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="detail-hook">I built [NAME] because I kept noticing the same gap. Being generous usually means one of two things: donating money or volunteering your time in a structured way. Both are genuinely great, and I'd encourage you to do both whenever you can. But neither covers everything. You can't donate your way into being there for your neighbours, or into being ready to help someone in an emergency. And if what you're in the mood for is something spontaneous, or something that fits into a hike or a pizza night rather than a formal commitment, that space is where some of the magic happens. This is an attempt to make it easier to unlock it.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="howto">
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>The idea is inspired by Chris Anderson's Infectious Generosity — the argument that generosity spreads fastest when it's easy to copy, genuinely enjoyable, and doesn't ask for a big sacrifice up front. I'd recommend it to everyone. This is an attempt to inspire and share knowledge and experiences on how we can a little more generous every day and what small actions can go a long way.</p>

      <h2>What this isn't</h2>
      <p>This deliberately isn't a volunteering platform, and it isn't a donation platform. Both of those are well served already, and if that's what you're looking for, [NAME] links out to good ones. Don’t get me wrong: I am a huge proponent of volunteering and giving to charity. Whatever you can give, however you can help. Please do check out those other resources.
What I am trying to serve here is the space in between: the free, thoughtful, often-overlooked things you can do with your own time, skills and attention, without routing them through an organisation or a payment. That's the gap this is attempting to sit in.
</p>

      <h2>Who built this</h2>
      <p>[NAME] is a small solo side project built by myself, Hanns Niedermark. I am mid-career-change from data and AI work toward climate, conservation and social impact. I am figuring a lot of this out the same way most people reading this are: one small thing at a time.
Importantly, this is a fun project I am building for everyone else, as much as myself. I have no ambition to turn this into a business or earn any money from this. This is entirely for knowledge sharing and to inspire each other to do a little more.
</p>

      <h2>More</h2>
      <p>
        Read the
        <a class="orglink" href={`${base}notes.html`}>notes</a> for occasional writing on how this is going, or drop me a note on [PLACEHOLDER] if you've got an idea worth adding, a correction, or just want to say hello.
I’ll need all the ideas, input, feedback and advice I can get to grow this.

      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
